# Secrets

Do not write passwords, tokens, or access keys in source, tests, YAML, or `.env`.

This pipeline authenticates with IAM. If a secret appears later, store the value in Secrets Manager and keep only its name in config. Build the ARN in code.

`AWS_ACCOUNT_ID` and certificate identifiers are not secrets. They still do not get copied from another project.

Replace the placeholder account `000000000000` in `.env` before a real deploy.
